Main's M25, answer 3: archive "the programme so far" byte for byte, with its three readers' checks and its appendix,
and write a short living page in plain words, every line with its source, as the README's first link. The new page is
read by one session that did not write it before the README points to it.

This patch is the first half: the page, for that reading.
- docs/THE_PROGRAMME_IN_SHORT.md (new): five short sections (the idea; the mathematics it builds; what it has
  obtained; what it has not obtained; where it stands), 15 lines of list, each ending in its source in brackets: a
  section of the full account (THE_PROGRAMME_SO_FAR.md, named by "§"), an item of GENESIS, or a page. No statement in
  it is new: each restates a sentence of the section it names. It uses no inner word of the public face's list. It is
  not on the public face's list and no page links to it.
- tests/test_the_programme_so_far.py: one test: every page the short page names exists, every section it names is a
  section of the full account, every line of its lists ends in a source, and it states the goal's count as the main
  goal's page does; the public face's count on it is zero. Three plants, each refused: a line with its source taken
  out, a section the full account lacks, a page that does not exist.

THE SECOND HALF, after the reading: the full account archived byte for byte beside itself (as the README's and the
main goal's were; a script, since it quotes a person), the short page's "§" pointed at the archive, the README's
first link moved to the short page, and the page put on the public face's list.

